      "id": "be-s6-linear-demand-tr-mr-c1",
      "heading": "Building the picture point by point",
      "explanation_md": "The deck builds one picture over several slides. The left graph has **price (P)** up to **100** and **quantity (Q)** from **0 to 50**: a straight downward demand line. The right graph shows **TR** against **Q**.\n\nPoints are added one at a time:\n\n| Price | Quantity | Total revenue |\n|---|---|---|\n| 80 | 10 | 800 |\n| 60 | 20 | 1200 |\n| 40 | 30 | 1200 |\n| 20 | 40 | 800 |\n\nSo as you slide down the demand line, **TR rises** (800, then 1200), is the same at Q = 20 and Q = 30, and then **falls** back to 800. The TR curve is a **hill shape** with its top between Q = 20 and Q = 30.",
      "example_ids": [
