    {
      "id": "be-s6-linear-demand-tr-mr-c2",
      "heading": "Elastic, unit elastic and inelastic zones",
      "explanation_md": "The last builds label the zones:\n\n- The **upper part** of the demand line (high price, low quantity) is **elastic**. Here TR is rising as Q rises.\n- The **middle point** where TR peaks is **unit elastic**.\n- The **lower part** (low price, high quantity) is **inelastic**. Here TR is falling as Q rises.\n\nThis matches the total revenue rules: in the elastic zone, cutting price raises TR; in the inelastic zone, cutting price lowers TR; at the top of the hill, demand is unit elastic. **One straight line has all three kinds of elasticity.**",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Along a linear demand curve: elastic at high prices, unit elastic at the TR peak, inelastic at low prices.",
      "clarification": null,
