    {
      "id": "be-s6-linear-demand-tr-mr-c3",
      "heading": "Marginal revenue and elasticity",
      "explanation_md": "The next slide adds the **MR** line to the same demand graph (the MR line is steeper and hits the quantity axis first).\n\nFor a **linear inverse demand function**: **MR(Q) = a + 2bQ**, where **b < 0**.\n\nThe zones are read from MR:\n\n- **MR > 0**: demand is **elastic**.\n- **MR = 0**: demand is **unit elastic**.\n- **MR < 0**: demand is **inelastic**.\n\nLink to TR: while MR is positive, TR is still rising; when MR hits zero, TR is at its peak.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
